---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import {
  VariantPop,
  VariantBloom,
  VariantMitosis,
  VariantDock,
  VariantWall,
} from '../../components/demo/BuildFleetLab.tsx';
---
<Site title="Lab · Build in parallel, as a fleet" noindex>
  <section class="home-build">
    <h1 class="plan-v-headline">Build in parallel — fleet concepts</h1>
    <p style="color: #86868b; max-width: 62ch; margin: 16px 0 0;">
      Scroll-scrubbed stages: each pins the viewport and grows the fleet with the wheel. The first two hold
      every tile still once it lands; the last three move them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="home-build" style="padding-bottom: 0;">
    <h2 class="plan-v-headline">7d · Pop</h2>
    <p style="color: #86868b; max-width: 62ch; margin: 12px 0 0;">
      Nothing reflows. Every tile lands at the size and slot it keeps for the rest of the section, scaling up
      from its own centre. The board is the finished board from the first frame — tiles only become visible.
    </p>
  </section>
  <VariantPop client:visible />

  <section class="home-build" style="padding-bottom: 0;">
    <h2 class="plan-v-headline">7e · Bloom</h2>
    <p style="color: #86868b; max-width: 62ch; margin: 12px 0 0;">
      The same no-reflow rule, arranged five-on-a-die: the lead terminal holds the centre and the rest pop in
      around it, so the fleet reads as having grown out of the middle without anything moving.
    </p>
  </section>
  <VariantBloom client:visible />

  <section class="home-build" style="padding-bottom: 0;">
    <h2 class="plan-v-headline">7a · Mitosis</h2>
    <p style="color: #86868b; max-width: 62ch; margin: 12px 0 0;">
      For contrast — the reflowing one. Seams open from nothing and every tile shrinks to make room.
    </p>
  </section>
  <VariantMitosis client:visible />

  <section class="home-build" style="padding-bottom: 0;">
    <h2 class="plan-v-headline">7b · Dock</h2>
    <p style="color: #86868b; max-width: 62ch; margin: 12px 0 0;">
      The lead tile settles from centre into its slot while the rest fly in from off stage.
    </p>
  </section>
  <VariantDock client:visible />

  <section class="home-build" style="padding-bottom: 0;">
    <h2 class="plan-v-headline">7c · Wall</h2>
    <p style="color: #86868b; max-width: 62ch; margin: 12px 0 0;">
      The camera opens inside the lead terminal and retreats until nine are in frame.
    </p>
  </section>
  <VariantWall client:visible />
</Site>
